Subject: gzguts.h: do not define _POSIX_C_SOURCE on OpenVMS

zlib 1.3 defines _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200112L in gzguts.h, after <stdio.h>.  With
the VSI C run-time library that makes <fcntl.h> declare creat() with two
parameters, conflicting with the variadic declaration <unixio.h> already
made, so gzclose.c (and the other gz*.c) failed with %CC-E-NOTCOMPAT.

--- a/gzguts.h	2026-10-03 21:55:10.713970078 +0100
+++ b/gzguts.h	2026-10-03 21:55:10.732924453 +0100
@@ -37,7 +37,11 @@
 #  include <limits.h>
 #endif
 
-#ifndef _POSIX_C_SOURCE
+/* OpenVMS: defining _POSIX_C_SOURCE here, after <stdio.h>, makes the CRTL's
+   <fcntl.h> declare creat() with a prototype that conflicts with the one
+   <unixio.h> already gave (%CC-E-NOTCOMPAT).  The CRTL declares what zlib
+   needs without it. */
+#if !defined(_POSIX_C_SOURCE) && !defined(__VMS)
 #  define _POSIX_C_SOURCE 200112L
 #endif
 #include <fcntl.h>
